
# ── WHY THIS FILE NOW CARRIES MORE THAN A CONTENT TYPE ────────────────────
#
# Six pages under web/ execute JavaScript fetched from a third party:
#
#     signup.html, join.html, coach.html, confirmed.html,
#     forgot-password.html, reset-password.html
#
# each `import`s @supabase/supabase-js from https://cdn.jsdelivr.net at a
# FLOATING major version (`@2`), with no Subresource Integrity — an ES module
# import cannot carry an `integrity` attribute — and, until this file said
# otherwise, with no Content-Security-Policy over it either.
#
# Those are precisely the pages where somebody types a password. Three of them
# are the account-creation and password-reset flows. Anything jsDelivr serves
# for that specifier runs with full access to those forms. That is the whole
# threat model in one sentence, and it had nothing in front of it.
#
# A CSP does not remove the dependency — only self-hosting that one file does,
# and that is worth doing. What it does is bound the blast radius: with the
# policy below, a compromised or substituted module still runs, but it cannot
# exfiltrate to an arbitrary host, because `connect-src` names the only two
# origins this site is allowed to talk to.
#
# ── WHY 'unsafe-inline' IS HERE, SAID PLAINLY ─────────────────────────────
#
# It is a real weakening and it is not decoration to admit it. Every page has
# an inline <script> for the phone nav, and there are 194 inline `style=`
# attributes across the site. Nonces need a server that renders per request;
# this directory has no build step and Cloudflare Pages serves it static, so
# there is nothing to generate one. Hashes would work for the scripts and would
# have to be regenerated on every edit to any page's <head> — a gate nobody
# would keep green, which this repo has learned is worse than no gate.
#
# So the honest position: script-src is 'self' + jsDelivr + inline, which stops
# script being pulled from any OTHER host, and the clauses that are absolute —
# frame-ancestors, object-src, base-uri, form-action — are the ones doing the
# structural work. Removing 'unsafe-inline' needs the inline scripts moved to
# files; that is a real change to twenty-two pages and it belongs in its own
# pass, not smuggled into a headers file overnight.
#
# ── WHAT EACH DIRECTIVE IS FOR ────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   default-src 'self'      nothing loads from anywhere unless named below
#   script-src              + jsDelivr, because six pages import from it
#   style-src / font-src    Google Fonts, which styles.css @imports
#   connect-src             the Supabase project, and nothing else. This is the
#                           clause that matters if the CDN module is ever bad.
#   img-src data:           the tick icon in styles.css is a data: URI
#   frame-ancestors 'none'  the site cannot be framed, so it cannot be clickjacked
#   form-action 'self'      a form cannot be repointed at somebody else's host
#   base-uri 'self'         <base> cannot be injected to re-root relative URLs
#   object-src 'none'       no plugins, ever
#
# Referrer-Policy is strict-origin-when-cross-origin so that the full path of
# the page a visitor is on is not handed to Google with the font request —
# they still learn the origin, which privacy.html now says out loud.
#
# HSTS deliberately WITHOUT includeSubDomains. A year-long max-age on the apex
# is safe and reversible-ish; extending it to every subdomain is a promise about
# hosts this file cannot see, and getting it wrong takes a subdomain off the air
# for a year with no way to tell a browser to forget it early. Add it when
# somebody has actually enumerated the subdomains and confirmed all are TLS.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://cdn.jsdelivr.net; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://phgfwzpkkwdysftlgkoq.supabase.co; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=(), interest-cohort=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000

# Apple refuses an association file that is not served as JSON, and this one
# deliberately has no .json extension, so nothing else infers the type for it.
/.well-known/apple-app-site-association
  Content-Type: application/json
